<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 26 December, from 795 to 2004.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">795 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,231 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leo III is elected pope</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Leo III was elected pope, becoming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and leader of the Papal States until his death in 816. On Christmas Day 800 he crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperator-romanorum">Emperor of the Romans</a> in St Peter's Basilica.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1606">1606 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">420 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Shakespeare's King Lear is performed before King James I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-shakespeare">William Shakespeare</a>'s tragedy King Lear, based on the legend of Leir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, was performed before King James I, the earliest performance on record, noted in the Stationers' Register. The play was probably written in late 1605 or early 1606.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-vi-and-i">James VI and I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1709">1709 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">317 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Handel's opera Agrippina premieres in Venice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-frideric-handel">George Frideric Handel</a>'s opera Agrippina, described as his first masterpiece, had its premiere in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. Its libretto by Cardinal Vincenzo Grimani followed Agrippina, mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a>, as she plotted the downfall of the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-frideric-handel">George Frideric Handel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington defeats the Hessians at Trenton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Washington's army surprised the Hessian garrison at Trenton, capturing about 900 soldiers with few American losses. The victory revived the Revolution after months of defeat.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1790">1790 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">236 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XVI assents to the Civil Constitution of the Clergy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having first opposed it, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a> gave his public assent to the Civil Constitution of the Clergy, which sought state control of the Catholic Church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The clergy's oaths followed, and the resulting schism lasted until 1801.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1825">1825 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">201 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Decembrist revolt fails in St Petersburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Army officers led troops onto Senate Square to refuse allegiance to Nicholas I and demand reform. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">Cannon</a> fire dispersed them; five leaders were hanged, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decembrists">Decembrists</a> inspired later Russian radicals.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1898">1898 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Curies announce the discovery of radium</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A paper presented to the French Academy of Sciences announced radium, a new element found in pitchblende by Marie and Pierre Curie with Gustave Bémont. It later proved vital in early cancer treatment.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2004">2004 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">22 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake and tsunami devastate the Indian Ocean</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 9.1 earthquake off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> sent tsunamis across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, killing about 230,000 people in 14 countries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> were worst hit.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a></div></div></li></ol>
